Without even knowing what Python 4 will look like, some parts of Astropy are guaranteed to be incompatible, e.g.

``` python
    def __lt__(self, other):
        if six.PY3:
            return super(Table, self).__lt__(other)
        elif six.PY2:
            raise TypeError("unorderable types: Table() < {0}".
                            format(str(type(other))))
```

in `table.py`. On Python 4, no code will get executed.

We should instead use:

``` python
if six.PY2:
    # Python 2 code
else:
    # Python 3 code
```

I wrote a short blog post about this: http://astrofrog.github.io/blog/2016/01/12/stop-writing-python-4-incompatible-code/ :)

