At some point, I implemented functionality to shorten the number of matrix operations in a long path of transformations with the frame transform graph when there are consecutive `StaticMatrixTransform`'s in the path (these can be combined into a single matrix operation). But, the combine was being done in the wrong order, leading to some very puzzling behavior that was noticed by @fardal in adrn/gala#109. Incidentally, this doesn't affect any of the transformations in astropy master (because there is only 1 `StaticMatrixTransform`: `SuperGalactic`), and only cropped up in Gala because all of the stream coordinate frames are `Static`.

Here's a working example of the current state:

```python
import astropy.coordinates as coord
import astropy.units as u
from astropy.coordinates.matrix_utilities import (rotation_matrix,
                                                  matrix_product,
                                                  matrix_transpose)
from astropy.coordinates.baseframe import frame_transform_graph
from astropy.coordinates.transformations import StaticMatrixTransform
from astropy.coordinates import representation as r
import numpy as np

class AFrame(coord.BaseCoordinateFrame):
